# MCP per-connection session isolation (fix shared-domain bleed)

Context: the MCP server binds ONE `MCPServerSession` to the FastMCP app for the
whole process. `selected_domain_name` and the label/class-Action caches lived on
that shared instance, so two clients hitting the one process clobbered each
other's selected domain — reproduced live on a deployed server: a
`mercuriamarkets` session returned `mercuriatrading` counts. This isolates that
state per MCP connection.

Changes:
1. `src/mcp-server/server/session_scope.py` (new): `CURRENT_SESSION_ID`
   context variable + `SessionScopeMiddleware.on_call_tool`, which binds each
   tool call to its `ctx.session_id` (guarded — `session_id` raises off-request)
   and resets it after. Imports nothing from `server.session` → no cycle.
2. `src/mcp-server/server/session.py`: moved `selected_domain_name`,
   `ontology_labels`, `class_actions` into a private `_DomainState`, held in an
   LRU-bounded `OrderedDict` keyed by session id (`_MAX_TRACKED_SESSIONS=512`).
   Exposed the three via properties resolving the current session's state, so
   every caller and existing test keeps the same API. `domain_policy`,
   `domain_has_graph`, `registry` and the pooled HTTP client stay server-wide.
3. `src/mcp-server/server/factory.py`:
   `mcp.add_middleware(SessionScopeMiddleware())`.
4. `tests/units/mcp/test_session_isolation.py` (new): regression guards —
   selected domain / caches do not leak between sessions, shared policy stays
   shared, store is LRU-bounded.

Modified files:
- src/mcp-server/server/session_scope.py (new)
- src/mcp-server/server/session.py
- src/mcp-server/server/factory.py
- tests/units/mcp/test_session_isolation.py (new)

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/mcp tests/mcp -m "not scenario"`
→ 107 passed (incl. 3 new isolation cases). Verified live on a deployed server:
concurrent trading + markets sessions each returned their own domain
(Position 1,536 vs 11,127), no cross-domain bleed.
